WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.650
<b>Forbidden Weapon</b>

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.110
<i>All my life, I staunchly believed...</i>

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.770
<i>that change doesn't happen 
at the drop of a hat.</i>

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:22.250
<i>Never did I imagine the entire world 
turning on its head in an instant.</i>

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.160
<i>Not in my wildest dreams.</i>

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.140
<i>Did... I do this?</i>

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:45.790
Yo, Natsume, give me your ID. 
I'll invite you to the next mixer.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.170
Uh, I don't have a cellphone.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:50.850
Are you for real? You're missing out, man.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.570
Just get a load of these chicks!

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.880
Can't believe how hot they are, can ya?

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.530
Huh? Natsume?!

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.340
And then?

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.770
One-way trip to the infirmary.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:05.960
Fried rice good to go!

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:11.330
Yeesh. I still can't get over 
how much you hate technology.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.700
Your cooking makes up for it, though.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.520
Yum! This is great!

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:21.420
It's nothing special compared 
to those dolls you make.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.350
Androids, you mean.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:24.720
Look.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:29.200
Just looking at it makes my head spin.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.150
My heart's racing, too.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.440
Y'know, maybe you just get too excited 
because you were born to love this stuff.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.780
Yeah, right.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:42.110
I think you should fight 
through the fear and dive into it.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.220
You never know. It might change something.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.030
Sounds convincing, given how you transformed.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.790
You used to be more of a weakling than me.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.800
How'd you do it? What's the secret?

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:52.890
Hard work!

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:53.790
What?

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.340
I went through hell after Mom and Dad passed.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.420
All thanks to my dear li'l bro here.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.010
I know, I know. 
And I'm thankful for all you've done.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:05.850
Akira.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.720
You've just gotta put your best foot forward.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.860
If you want to change, that is.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.360
We are a go.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.080
<i>"Put my best foot forward," huh?</i>

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.500
<i>Easier said than done.</i>

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.060
Let me go!

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:34.720
C'mon. It won't kill you.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.000
Where do you live? We'll walk you.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.460
Stop!

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.320
Come on.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.290
<i>What do I do? I should help her out, 
shouldn't I?</i>

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:44.490
<i>No, there's three of them. 
I don't stand a chance.</i>

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.000
<i>But am I just gonna walk away? 
Remember what your big bro just said?</i>

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.000
Akira.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.270
You've just gotta put your best foot forward.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.200
If you want to change, that is.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.600
Oh, to hell with it!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.440
Here goes Akira!

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.200
<i>And that's the last of my memories.</i>

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:13.920
<i>Emergency alert.</i>

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.380
<i>An agent's currently engaging 
a group of smugglers.</i>

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:17.660
<i>All units provide backup!</i>

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.520
Get that thing back!

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.420
There!

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.170
Minami.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.370
Alma!

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.230
Shit!

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.360
Hold it!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:56.760
Alma!

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.970
Is she... an android?!

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:50.840
Damn it!

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.770
Come in, HQ! We've secured the trunk!

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.550
<i>Listen up. 
That's what we've been looking for.</i>

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:06.730
It is?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.520
<i>Hold on to it until backup arrives.</i>

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:09.450
Roger!

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.950
Find 'em! They should be in here!

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:16.760
The ship set sail?

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:17.920
Looks like it.

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:20.460
Out of the frying pan, into the fire...

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:25.050
Hey, this thing's supposed to be 
some kind of crazy weapon, right?

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.750
Please don't get any funny ideas.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.320
It's top-secret classified information.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:31.820
Yeah, well, that's not gonna keep me alive.

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:34.540
It's time to sink or swim!

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.810
<i>Huh?</i>

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:50.570
<i>I... I can't feel my body.</i>

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.270
<i>Where am I? I can't see a thing.</i>

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:56.440
<i>Device connected. Come in, EX-ARM.</i>

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.550
<i>Whoa, what was that?</i>

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:01.800
<i>What the hell?!</i>

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.500
It talked!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.920
You talked to me first!

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.490
Wait, who even are you?

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:11.180
You first. Who are <i>you</i>?

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.940
Me? I'm...

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:17.200
Me?!

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:20.540
My name's Natsume Akira!

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:24.510
Minami, these aren't an AI's brain waves.

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:26.410
This is an actual human brain.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:28.940
Huh? That can't be!

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.910
Hey, what are you talking about?

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:34.860
I mean, you don't look human at all.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:35.840
See?

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:36.930
Huh?

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:41.040
Wait, this contraption is me?!

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:45.790
To be more precise, it's a human brain 
encased in a titanium shell.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.260
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:50.440
Why can I see myself, then?

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.460
Oh, quit yapping.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:55.780
Alma's sharing her visual data right now.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:56.730
Huh?

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.700
I'm Uezono Minami. Nice to meetcha.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.960
Sharing... visual data?

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.050
How is that possible?

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:07.830
Well, Alma is an android.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.300
An android?!

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.120
Yes.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:21.360
An Alma-series prototype co-developed by the MPD 
and Irie Heavy Industries in 2028.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.580
Hold up. Timeout.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.170
What do you mean, 2028?

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.350
Isn't it 2014 right now?

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:31.610
What? It's 2030!

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:34.840
2... 2030?!

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:39.870
It would appear you spent 
the last 16 years in a coma.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:45.620
<i>Yeah, nope. None of this makes any sense.</i>

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:48.570
<i>Is this real life?</i>

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.580
<i>It's gotta be a dream of some sort, right?</i>

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:58.570
Uezono and Alma stole the thing 
and ran onto their ship.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:01.520
Great. More work to do for us.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.060
Want us to help, then?

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:06.350
Wanibuchi, Miyabe...

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:08.750
We're not working with Public Safety.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.850
Orders from the top, unfortunately.

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:14.010
The briefing's about to begin.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:22.180
Given that, we can assume that 
what the smugglers were dealing at the harbor...

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.330
was an EX-ARM.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:30.310
A weapon series with no info. 
Not who developed it, nor how it was distributed.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:32.480
Found 'em!

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:37.940
Its capabilities far exceed 
what technology in 2030 can produce.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:39.860
This is the police!

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:46.460
Be it the escalating mafia wars of recent times, 
or several other violent crimes,

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:49.530
EX-ARM's shadow looms large over all of them.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:53.550
Should you ever run into anyone 
with one of them,

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:55.170
run away immediately.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:56.310
Fire!

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:03.210
Because normal weapons don't stand a chance 
against them.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:06.940
That's how terrifying the EX-ARM are.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:11.460
Hey, EX-ARM.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:13.360
Again, I'm...

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.680
You're a crazy weapon, right?

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:19.210
Hurry up and show us what you can do, EX-ARM.

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.960
Again, my name's Natsume Akira!

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:24.040
I'm a person, not a weapon!

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.000
Think we can use him, Alma?

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.840
No. It's a real human brain.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:34.860
I don't believe it has a way 
of getting us out of this situation.

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.460
What? But it was our last resort.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:39.690
Hold up.

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:43.470
Use me? "Last resort"? What's all this about?

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:44.890
What the hell are <i>you</i> supposed to be?

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:47.130
What? Isn't it obvious?

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:48.700
We're the police.

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.360
P-Police?!

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:55.100
Yep. We're aboard the ship of a group 
of smugglers after you and us.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:57.520
<i>S-Smugglers?!</i>

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.280
<i>Forget it. I'm done.</i>

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.010
Looks like he really is just some rando.

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:03.950
Don't call me a "rando"!

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:04.740
Minami!

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:07.030
Found you.

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:13.960
What the? Did he just slip through the wall?!

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.050
How?

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:23.350
It's futile.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:26.270
Physical attacks can't harm me.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.050
Wait, that number...

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:34.560
Indeed.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:37.990
EX-ARM Number 08.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:40.280
The Throughhand.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:45.260
Wow, you managed to boot that thing?

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:48.950
If you hand it over, 
I don't mind letting you two go.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.370
No way, pal!

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.240
Why not? It's just a brain.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:56.270
He looks wack,

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:58.210
but he's a real, live human being!

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:01.380
So we'll protect him!

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.040
You...

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:05.840
Hmph. In that case...

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.970
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.980
How am I supposed to believe any of this?

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:16.730
This wacky contraption is me?

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.330
What the hell happened?

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:22.270
<i>And</i> you're telling me it's 2030 now, 
and we're on a smuggling group's ship?!

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:23.050
Pull my nonexistent leg!

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.520
Oh, shut your mouth! Keep it down!

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:28.160
'Scuse me? My mouth's all I've got!

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:28.810
Freeze!

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:31.500
Whoa, what are you doing?!

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.410
Don't worry. Titanium is tough.

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:37.530
Caught you.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:41.800
Take him and run!

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:42.430
Got it.

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:43.770
Hey, wait!

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:45.980
That's one smart android.

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:46.880
Not so fast!

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:51.260
I guess I'll cook you up first.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.760
Find 'em!

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:55.790
They won't find us up here.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.440
Hey, we need to go help her.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:13:59.860
That's the plan, yes.

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:02.910
I connected you 
to the ship's network cabling.

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.230
You should be able to see now.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.800
See what?

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:07.200
CC footage and stuff?

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.410
Uh, I don't see a thing.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:12.520
But you accessed my visual data 
easily earlier.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:15.640
Hmm... If there's no
overarching command system,

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.600
maybe you'll be able to, if you try to see.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:19.660
Later.

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:23.000
Oh, come on! 
What are you asking me to do?!

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.770
Did you know?

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:32.550
Organs are still a hot product 
for us smugglers.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.950
I'll slice and dice you up real nice.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.360
Alma! I told you to run!

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:45.880
You're disobeying orders here!

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.800
You're one to talk.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.680
Let me see! Come on!

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:54.720
Shit, I can't see a thing! Damn it all!

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:57.800
I've been left all alone 
in this crazy situation.

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:02.410
Am I gonna be completely useless yet again?!

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:04.540
Akira.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.670
You've just gotta put your best foot forward.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.710
If you want to change, that is.

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.000
<i>Bro...</i>

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:13.160
<i>Wait, what's happening?</i>

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:19.180
<i>I can see CC footage now.</i>

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:21.290
<i>It's not just vision.</i>

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:23.530
<i>All my senses are coming back...</i>

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.880
<i>to the body I couldn't feel until now.</i>

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:28.650
Huh? I can move my body now!

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:31.590
I'm filling up with power!

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.650
I don't have a foot to put forward anymore,

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:38.640
but that also means I can't run away.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:39.830
Which means...

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:43.020
My only option is to do this!

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:08.940
All the power and speed in the world 
mean nothing if you can't touch me.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.020
Alma!

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:10.190
Game over.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:18.600
The ship's network is being
bombarded with traffic!

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:19.870
We can't control it!

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:21.290
What? Why are the sprinklers...

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.330
Shit! The hatch's been locked!

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:30.310
It feels like this entire ship 
has become my body.

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:34.670
Where are those two? I need to find them.

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:35.720
There!

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:38.380
Is it you?

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:40.940
You're okay?

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:45.020
No. My mobility chip seems 
to have been damaged.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.050
So I have a favor to ask.

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:51.430
Access my AI and take control of my body.

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:55.610
We shared my vision smoothly earlier.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.240
I'm sure you can do this, too.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:00.440
But... I've always had a thing against tech.

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:02.600
Always felt like the machines 
would suck me in.

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:06.490
Stop it, you freak!

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:08.880
Settle down or I'll kill you.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:15.770
Hurry up and get inside me!

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:21.540
Come on!

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.620
<i>Looks like it worked.</i>

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:30.110
<i>Now stand up.</i>

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:35.320
<i>Just like with the ship. I can do this.</i>

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:41.470
Don't push your luck, you freak!

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:44.870
Alma...?

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:48.120
You can still move? I'll break you for good.

00:17:57.480 --> 00:17:59.300
Damn, I can't control myself.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:03.950
<i>Don't overthink it.</i>

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:06.770
<i>You took over my body extremely naturally.</i>

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:09.800
<i>You probably already have the protocols.</i>

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:11.040
<i>I know.</i>

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:14.200
<i>I've just gotta picture what I wanna do.</i>

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:16.150
<i>Picture it.</i>

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:20.460
<i>Picture myself as the hero 
in a kung-fu movie!</i>

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:42.490
What's with you? You seem different, Alma.

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:44.840
Nah, it's your boy here.

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:45.720
Huh?

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:48.140
You're not getting away!

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.060
Yes!

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:01.660
Wait, is the other side of this wall...

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:04.620
Exactly. It's the sea.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.340
It was noticeable while fighting you.

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:10.060
You blocked kicks from behind.

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:12.710
You took the body hit from the side.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:14.790
Your little EX-ARM

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:18.220
only affects the area in front of you.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:20.760
You can't slip through backward.

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:23.970
You can escape through that wall 
if you want, but then you'll just sink.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:30.010
Wow, you're pretty smart.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:33.400
Actually, Alma told me all this.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.530
What the heck? 
I'm taking back the compliment.

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:38.890
Come on! Be thankful 
I fixed this mess for you!

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:42.000
"Fixed," you say?

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:44.370
You people don't understand a thing.

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:51.240
You know that EX-ARM has taken over 
underworlds everywhere, right?

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:54.350
Then you should know 
that it's already too late.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:58.920
Mankind can't let go of powers 
it has obtained.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:03.160
And EX-ARM is the ultimate power. 
It makes its wielders superior.

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:06.350
The strong will take from the weak, 
and the weak will die.

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:09.420
Nobody can break that cycle now.

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:13.140
You're wrong!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:19.400
The strong must use their powers 
to protect the weak!

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:41.080
Well, that's case closed.

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:42.990
Thank god.

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:44.410
Chief Shiga?!

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.330
Good job on this operation.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.010
So this is Number 00...

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:52.780
Uezono Minami, Alma.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:57.020
Normally, you would be disciplined 
for disobeying orders,

00:20:57.020 --> 00:21:02.190
but I'll let it slide, 
in light of your capture of EX-ARM 08.

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:08.560
Wait. I'm, uh... not Alma.

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:10.520
I know it probably doesn't make any sense.

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:11.870
Don't move. On your knees.

00:21:14.180 --> 00:21:18.220
Please. This thing isn't who I am.

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:21.700
I'm human! Help me!

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:28.630
It's been ten years since that terrible tragedy, 
but you're still...

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.530
an enemy of mankind.

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:46.280
<i>Is that... me?</i>

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:49.960
<i>I'm...</i>

00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>an enemy of all mankind?</i>

00:23:25.640 --> 00:23:26.750
Oh, come on!

00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:29.580
Why'd I become a brain in a machine? 
I hate technology!

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:31.640
And I'm a weapon now?

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:34.180
What? The Counter EX-ARM Squad?

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:36.910
Next time, on <i>EX-ARM:</i> 
"Battle 002 - Day of Judgment."

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Day of Judgment</b>

00:23:36.910 --> 00:23:39.290
Wait, I've gotta solve a case?!
